  "body": "## Summary\n\n- Update the supported Minecraft version to 1.26.40 / protocol 2168.\n- Implement the v2168 Cereal discriminators and optional wrappers across entity metadata, inventory, movement, player, score, map, skin, sound, chunk, and resource-pack payloads.\n- Migrate crafting data to the v2168 typed recipe vectors and update item/descriptor wire formats.\n- Add the new protocol fields, ordinals, particles, sounds, and memory categories.\n- Align the new codecs with existing gophertunnel IO and Marshal patterns, removing transitional compatibility state and duplicate recipe/item codecs.\n\n## Protocol references\n\n- [CloudburstMC exact v2168 codec](https://github.com/CloudburstMC/Protocol/blob/19e31c33dc424b2b7e0098e0cbd9aae208705c2b/bedrock-codec/src/main/java/org/cloudburstmc/protocol/bedrock/codec/v2168/Bedrock_v2168.java)\n- [CloudburstMC v2168 gatherings codec](https://github.com/CloudburstMC/Protocol/blob/19e31c33dc424b2b7e0098e0cbd9aae208705c2b/bedrock-codec/src/main/java/org/cloudburstmc/protocol/bedrock/codec/v2168/BedrockCodecHelper_v2168.java#L1166-L1191)\n- [Mojang r/26_u4 changelog](https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/blob/7330880ab78ef001cad0b9cdfedb3aa3eaa6d4af/changelog_2168_07_07_26.md)\n- [Mojang automated 1.26.40 gatherings schema](https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/blob/0e00fe80f4f3c71572ff6429de40146d1f4412fc/json/gatheringsConfig.json)\n- [Mojang automated 1.26.40 sound-update schema](https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/blob/0e00fe80f4f3c71572ff6429de40146d1f4412fc/json/ClientboundUpdateSoundDataPacketPayload.json)\n- [Mojang automated 1.26.40 Fade payload](https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/blob/0e00fe80f4f3c71572ff6429de40146d1f4412fc/json/Fade.json)\n- [TwistedAsylumMC/bpd-fixer](https://github.com/TwistedAsylumMC/bpd-fixer)\n\nThe merged Mojang r/26_u4 metadata identifies protocol 2169 / Minecraft 1.26.50, while the pinned `automated/1.26.40` branch identifies protocol 2168 and is used for exact-version field order and union layout. In particular, every `ClientboundUpdateSoundData` slot is an independent seven-way union and `Fade` encodes `Duration` before `Target Volume`; Cloudburst's v2168 serializer hardcodes selector 0 and reverses those fields, so it is not followed for that packet.\n\nMojang's `gatheringsConfig` schema marks all eight fields required, and bpd-fixer currently leaves that metadata unchanged. Cloudburst's exact v2168 read/write codec instead shows optional markers for `worldId`, `worldName`, `targetId`, `scenarioId`, and `serverId`; this PR follows that wire codec while keeping `experienceId`, `experienceName`, and `creatorId` required.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `go test ./... -count=1`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Independent exact-version review against Mojang `automated/1.26.40`, Cloudburst v2168, and the corrected bpd-fixer schema\n- GitHub Actions: passing\n\nNo new test files are included in this PR.\n",
